"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boissel</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Zelenka</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Godtel-Armbrust</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Feuerstein</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Forstermann</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transcription of different exons 1 of the human neuronal nitric oxide synthase gene is dynamically regulated in a cell- and stimulus-specific manner</article-title><source>Biol Chem</source><year>2003</year><volume>384</volume><fpage>351</fpage><lpage>362</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1515/BC.2003.041</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Boissel JP, Zelenka M, Godtel-Armbrust U, Feuerstein TJ, Forstermann U (2003) Transcription of different exons 1 of the human neuronal nitric oxide synthase gene is dynamically regulated in a cell- and stimulus-specific manner. Biol Chem 384:351&#x02013;362. doi:10.1515/BC.2003.041 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12715886</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boucher</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Moali</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tenu</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nitric oxide biosynthesis, nitric oxide synthase inhibitors and arginase competition for L-arginine utilization</article-title><source>Cell Mol Life Sci</source><year>1999</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>1015</fpage><lpage>1028</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s000180050352</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Boucher JL, Moali C, Tenu JP (1999) Nitric oxide biosynthesis, nitric oxide synthase inhibitors and arginase competition for L-arginine utilization. Cell Mo